                <pb facs="1214" n="1120" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg1120"/>

                <head>No. 694.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Straus</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from the consul of the United States at Smyrna, No. 27, of July 8,
                    1887, relative to the status of descendants of American citizens born in Turkey;
                    also a copy of Department’s reply, No. 22, of the 9th instant, calling his
                    attention to the Department’s instruction of April 20, 1887, No. 7, upon the
                    general subject of the rights of American citizens in the Ottoman dominions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>






